  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1004.04 Alteration of Subdivisions After Approval",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1004.04 Alteration of Subdivisions After Approval.\n\n(a) The plan for a subdivision approved by the department shall be the final plan.\n\n(b) If a lot line changes and a new 4,000 SF area is required pursuant to Env-Wq 1005.02(b)(2), a new application with a plan shall be submitted for approval, unless exempted by RSA 485-A:33, I-III.\n\n(c) If a lot line changes but a new 4,000 SF is not required pursuant to Env-Wq 1005.02(b)(2), an amended plan shall be submitted to the department, unless exempted by RSA 485-A:33, I-III.\n\n(d) For both (b) and (c), above, each lot shall meet the requirements of Env-Wq 1005 and the plan shall meet the requirements of Env-Wq 1003.07.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1 and #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1000) #11184, eff 10-1-16; ss by #14486, eff 2-1-26, EXPIRES: 2-1-36 (formerly Env-Wq 1004.05)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1000.html"
